meta {
  name: List scheduled items
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/scheduled-items
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~kind: bill
  ~accountId: acc_chequing
  ~status: active
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  A scheduled item is a **rule, not a row**: `startDate` + `frequency` generate
  dates on demand, so editing an item instantly changes the whole forecast and
  there is no queue of stale future rows. `nextDueDate` is derived on read, so it
  cannot go stale. The cost of not materialising: "mark this one paid" lives in
  `postedOccurrences` and `skippedDates`, keyed by date.
  
  18 items in the seed, including one paused (`sch_meal_kit`) and one anchored to
  the 31st (`sch_water`, quarterly — watch it clamp in February).
}
